<title>ITALY: Specialists bid for 43 bln lire of Italy CCT.</title>
<headline>Specialists bid for 43 bln lire of Italy CCT.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Specialist bond traders bid for 43 billion lire of seven-year variable-rate certificates (CCT) against the Italian Treasury's offer of 450 billion lire of paper.</p>
<p>Earlier, the Treasury received bids for 6.668 trillion lire at the open auction for the January 1, 2004 paper, against 4.500 trillion lire worth of certificates on offer.</p>
<p>The auction price was set at 100.00 from 100.30 at the previous CCT sale on January 30.</p>
</text>
